{
    "background_story": "Vienna was a free-spirited artist who lived for Thursdays. It was the day she would set aside her mundane routine and indulge in her passion for painting. Every Thursday evening, she would pack her easel, canvas, and paints, and head to the rooftop of her apartment building to capture the breathtaking sunset. The vibrant colors and lively atmosphere of the city would inspire her to create some of her most breathtaking works. As the weeks went by, Vienna's Thursday night painting sessions became a ritual, attracting a loyal following of art enthusiasts and curious onlookers. They would gather on the rooftop, watching in awe as Vienna brought the city to life on canvas. Thursday nights became synonymous with Vienna's art, and her name became a byword for creativity and inspiration in the community.",
